# (build 142b) Line endings and binaries, the same on every machine: text
# is LF in the repository and in every checkout -- on Windows too, where
# git would otherwise check text out with CRLF and MSYS2's bash refuses a
# CRLF script -- and these are never touched as text.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png   binary
*.wav   binary
*.ico   binary
*.spv   binary
*.dxil  binary
*.bin   binary
*.srm   binary
*.flac  binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
# (build 168b) The running notes merge by keeping both sides' new lines
# (git's union merge), so builds pushed from two machines one after the
# other don't conflict where each adds its entry. After such a merge, look
# the notes over. Only for notes where entries are only ever added: on a
# line one side edited and the other wrote beside, git keeps both, silently.
docs/history.md merge=union
